From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: llama: ragged recurrent batches with in-place SSM state

For serving hundreds of Nemotron-H sequences of different lengths, with
llama_serving_params.batched (Nemotron-H MoE, unified KV cache):

- split_ragged packs sequences of unequal length into one ubatch described by
  seq_offsets. The Mamba2 layer uses the ragged conv and scan ops, chunked SSD
  for long segments, and the fused conv bias + SiLU and gate norm.
- Recurrent state stays in place: one pinned F16 cell per sequence, read and
  written directly by the scan, with ReplaySSM rows for one-token decode.
  MTP verify steps (mtp_replay) append uncommitted rows and the next step
  commits only the accepted tokens.
- The KV length is padded to kv_bucket so decode graphs are reused, and the
  masks reserved at init cover at most kv_reserve_cells cells.
- O(1) seq_pos_min/max and batch-allocator fast paths for many sequences.

Upstream: not planned in this form (Nemotron-H only).

